            <h1>6. Moral Panics & Societal Fears</h1>
        </header>

        <section class="dossier-case-summary">
            <p>Many urban legends are manifestations of "Moral Panics"—generalized fears that someone or something threatens the values of society. Tales of organ harvesting, poisoned Halloween candy, or kidnapping rings in white vans reflect deep-seated mistrust in strangers and institutional decay. This dimension explores how these legends are weaponized during periods of social change. It analyzes the role of the media in amplifying these myths, often leading to real-world hysteria and legal repercussions despite a lack of evidence.</p>
        </section>

